- **[main.tscn](mdc:main.tscn)**: main scene
- **[openxr_action_map.tres](mdc:openxr_action_map.tres)**: VR input mapping
- **[default_bus_layout.tres](mdc:default_bus_layout.tres)**: Master, Music (ducked under Voice), SFX, Voice, Critical, UI

## Collision Layers
- **1** world
- **2** hands (strike spheres, mask phantoms)
- **3** phantoms (punchable bodies)
- **4** phantom_sensors (contact areas, mask world/player body)
- **5** ui

## Signal Flow
Phantom `resolved` / `player_contact` / `strike_rejected` → RiftManager → RiftDirector → RoundController (score, chain, life force) → HUD, ChenComms, MusicIntensityController. RoundController `round_finished` → GameFlowController → VRMenuPresenter results.

## Development Guidelines
- Follow Godot 4.x best practices; typed GDScript; signals over polling
- Find systems by group (`Player`, `PlayerBody`, `RoundController`, `RiftSpawnManager`, `LifeForceManager`, `VRMenuPresenter`, `CombatVFX`, `ChenComms`, `PhantomContainer`)
- Keep gameplay numbers in exports or the mission catalog; presentation reads signals and never owns state
- One mesh per creature and per set piece; no per-phantom raycasts or allocations in steady state; prewarm shaders during the menu
- Keep the desktop fallback working (`--xr-mode off`) so flow and art can be checked without a headset
- Run `tools/validate_project.sh` before committing gameplay or scene changes
- Record headset sessions in `development/Playtest_Log.md`
- Document design and production changes in `development/`
